    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. Independently: q-160402 has Jacobian e^{u-v}(1/v+1/u), giving 2; q-160440 has Jacobian -sin(u)cos(v), giving -1/2. For q-161877 and q-161788, the determinants at the specified points are -3 and -26, so the approximate image areas are 3δA and 26δA. For q-161842, the determinant is v-u², so orientation reverses below the parabola, matching option 3. For q-161837, the determinant is u³-v, so orientation reverses above the cubic, matching option 4. Divergence gives 1/x+x for q-131171, 3√(x²+y²)=15 for q-131174, ye^z+ln(y)+xe^z+x+1=4 for q-131179, and 6xyz=24 for q-123192. For q-107999, v dv/dx=4x and v(2)=8 give v²=4x²+48; increasing displacement selects the positive root. For q-122325, integrating dx/dt=e^{-2x} with x(0)=0 gives x(t)=ln(2t+1)/2. All cross partials vanish for q-131338, giving the zero vector. For q-98894, curl is (ze^x-xye^z,-yze^x,ye^z), giving (1,-2,2e). The scalar curls Q_x-P_y are 2xy/(x²+1)-2y, giving 2 for q-126520, and 2-x cos(y) for q-126537. No earlier submitted answers or grades are supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent calculations.",
